<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=camera-obscura">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Science and discovery</p><h1 class="enc-title">Camera obscura</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A camera obscura is a dark chamber or box in which light passing through a small hole projects an inverted image of the scene outside onto the opposite surface; one of the earliest known written records of the effect is the Chinese text Mozi, of the 4th century BCE. Ibn al-Haytham studied it extensively in the early 11th century. Fitted with a lens from the second half of the 16th century, it became a popular drawing aid, and in the first half of the 19th century it developed into the photographic camera.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/camera-obscura.jpg" alt="Camera obscura" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Athanasius Kircher · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1646_Athanasius_Kircher_-_Camera_obscura.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>4th century BCE</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>China</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Mozi · <a href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Also arose independently</span>Greece (Aristotle’s school) (4th century BCE)</p><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>The article mentions possible earlier traces: perforated gnomons projecting a pinhole image of the sun in the Chinese Zhoubi Suanjing (1046 BC–256 BC, with material added until c. 220 AD), and theories that camera obscura effects inspired Paleolithic cave paintings or played a role in Neolithic structures.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/photography">Photography<span>1826–1827</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=camera-obscura">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
